WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.920
- Acquiring professional certificates

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.420
can be quite time consuming.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.090
It can take quite a lot
of effort to get them.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.200
So today, in this video,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.880
I wanna inquire the question

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.490
what the most important certificates

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.250
for business professionals really are.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.810
So, welcome to another coffee break

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:17.640
here on my channel Firm Learning.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.780
My name is Heinrich

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.580
I'm a former McKinsey consultant

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.780
and on my channel I talk about

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.320
how to become successful in
the first years of your career.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.810
So this video is informed by
my six years in consulting,

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.150
having seen lots of
companies in that time,

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.910
and I also asked you on
Instagram to get your opinion

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.610
what the most important
certificates are and why.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.890
So all of this has been
gone into this video.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:38.850
But to get some clarity

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.350
of what it is that I'm talking about

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.730
let's mention four areas

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.560
that I will not cover in this video.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.710
And the first are very
regular university degrees

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.230
something like a bachelor,
a master, an MBA.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.700
This is not what I will talk about.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.770
This is not what I'm
considering a certificate.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.810
Same is true for
professional certifications

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.510
that you just need to
work on a specific job.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:00.180
This for instance is a bar exam in law.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.180
I'm also not including a CPA or an ACCA

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.400
or any other accounting
certification like that.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.380
Next, I will not consider certifications

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.390
that are very specific to IT.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.990
So SAP certifications,
certifications from Google.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.120
And finally, I will also
not include certifications

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.300
that are very specific to
just one sub-area of business,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.400
something like a CPIM in supply chain

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.110
or a CMA in accounting.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.580
And again, exception would be those

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.773
that are more broadly
recognized and applicable.

00:01:25.773 --> 00:01:29.460
With that being said, let's
jump here into our tier list

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.220
With the S tier being the highest tier

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.590
and the D tier being the lowest tier

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.150
here in the rank that we are going to do.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.740
And now let's start with certifications

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.220
from platforms like Udacity
or Coursera and so on.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.960
And those for me are platforms

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.520
where you do get a certificate

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.290
through a structured online course

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:50.040
and there are some type of
examination logic in the end

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.070
where not everyone
necessarily gets a certificate

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.720
that goes over the curriculum.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.380
And I'm placing these types
of certificates in the C tier.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.760
And my rational here is that,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.400
yes, often you learn
quite a lot of things.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.270
It can be really helpful

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.550
Also myself once took a Udacity course

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.070
and I did learn a lot of things from that.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.110
Though the truth is I would still argue

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.120
that these types of courses are not

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.220
that respected by employers.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.870
There's not really the
perception behind it

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.310
that you have such a certificate.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.230
You're already an expert in this field.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.170
You really accomplish something
significant if you pass.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.790
So yes, you will learn good things,

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.440
but no, I do not think that this will make

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.180
a huge impact on your career.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.460
Next, let's talk about
SCRUM Master certifications

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.490
and for the uninitiated,
the SCRUM master is a role

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.800
in the agile methodology of news,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.680
for instance, in modern
software development.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.170
I place this in the C tier for the reasons

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.060
that on one side, this is I think,

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.310
a skill that is not that narrow.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.800
I think you can apply agile methodologies

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.170
in many different areas in business.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.210
Not only, for instance
in software development.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.340
And I do think that this whole trend

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.980
towards moving to agile is very valuable

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.100
and many businesses cherish
this and value this.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.010
And especially this idea
of being a SCRUM master

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.490
is something with some positive
connotation tied to it.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.260
There's several quite
renowned institutions

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.930
where you can do a SCRUM
master certification.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.610
As long as you pick one of them.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.080
I don't think you'll make huge steps

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.030
in your career only because of that.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.730
But I think it is very
much worth checking it out.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.200
Quite similar to the SCRUM master,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.720
I see the 6 Sigma Belts certifications.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.080
So this is a principle of
an applied in production

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.000
It is about process quality.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.220
It is about continuous improvement.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.480
And this is something that I think

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.820
many people know, many people know about.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.920
It's a system where you
start with a white belt

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.900
and then it can advance
up to a black belt.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.330
I think the last one is a master belt.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.010
It is something that many people know.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.860
I think the 6 Sigma principles
are very well applicable

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.720
in many different types of business

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.400
outside of production as well.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.290
And people will respect it if you say

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.540
that you are a 6 Sigma black belt.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.700
Next to talk about
language certifications,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.910
like the TOEFL, like the
IELTS certifications,

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.430
where you prove that
your language abilities

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.050
meet a certain level.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.730
And these types of
certifications are actually

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.590
often required to get for instance,

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:08.700
into master degrees,
also into MBA programs.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.440
The reason why I put them into the D tier

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.970
is not that they are worthless.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.860
Sure they can help to prove

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.510
we have one of these certifications.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:16.770
And then of course you would like to have

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.590
a nice high score to
really make use of it.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.760
It's nice to use this,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.260
to prove that your English skills

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.420
are really meeting very high standards,

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:25.560
but the truth is also,

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:28.200
especially for these
high-paced career roads

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.760
in IB, in consulting,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.430
if applying to a firm
like McKinsey, BCG, Bain,

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.140
people will just assume

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.600
that you have very good English skills.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.100
It's not really something

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.690
where people will test you for.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.610
Some consulting firms do decide to have

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.860
just an English component
in one of the interviews,

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.780
where they just converse
with you in English,

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:47.520
to see whether you're up to the level.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.110
But if you pass this,

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.880
usually you will get the check box

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.290
and then it doesn't really matter

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.620
how high exactly your
TOEFL score was in the end.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.300
Next, let's talk about the PMP,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.360
the Project Management
Professional certification.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.460
This is the certification where you prove

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.800
that you have project management skills.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.210
That you can lead teams,

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.850
understand what stakeholder
management is all about.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.570
Master the common project
management skills and abilities.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.800
And this is one where I'd say,

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.290
this is very well known, well respected.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.300
People will know usually what this is.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.430
And then on the other hand,
there's also the fact that

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.250
in almost all modern business roads,

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.770
there will be some type
of project management

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:26.610
expected from you.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.020
This is surely true in consulting,

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.060
but also if you work in industry,

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.860
project management is just part

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:34.860
of almost every modern business role,

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.050
which is, I believe, it
is just very important,

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.630
very relevant and also
quite very respected.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:43.710
So this should justify the A
tier for the PMP certification.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.140
And now let's talk about
another certification

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.940
that I will place in the A tier.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:52.650
And this is the CASE Score.
The Candidate Select Score.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.390
And Candidate Select is actually

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:57.060
the sponsor of today's video.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.950
So what are they solving?

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.900
Put yourself on the shoes of a student.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.060
You studied at one of the prestigious

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.710
Target business schools

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:08.670
and maybe you score on
the top 10% of your cohort

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:11.970
at this prestigious
Target business school.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.560
But are you now just in general

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.020
in the top 10% of business students?

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.690
Well, likely not. Likely
you are much better, right?

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.730
Likely your percentage will be much higher

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.460
because of course there's
already a pre-selection

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:28.080
of students attending this
specific Target business school.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.740
It wouldn't be fair to compare
yourself to another person.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:36.150
The top 10% of maybe a
Non-Target business school.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.010
And these are exactly the considerations

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:41.460
that CASE wants to solve with
their certification program.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.470
Because CASE is the provider of a fair

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.410
and objective evaluation
of university degrees,

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.290
both for students and also for employers.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.110
And they do this by collecting
lots of great distributions

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.150
for many, many universities and degrees,

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:59.150
and combine this with over
400,000 data points of IQ tests

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.920
and personality tests
to algorithmically put

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.110
all the grades in the right context.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.880
So with CASE you can get a certificate

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.390
as the proof of your actual
academic performance.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.520
Above and beyond just the absolute great.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.500
And the truth is that many companies,

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.990
including Boston Consulting Group,

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:19.920
Kearney, Airbus, Thyssenkrupp,
among many others,

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.720
they respect this certification.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.690
Actually, encourage applicants to apply

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:26.850
with this certification to the job.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.410
The CASE certificate is currently offered

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.090
for eight different countries.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.420
This includes Germany, China, India, Italy

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.420
Portugal, Spain, UK, and USA.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:38.340
So if you're interested
for the certificate,

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:41.280
CASE provided a link for
the Firm Learning community.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.680
We can actually get the basic version

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.770
of this certificate completely for free.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.230
Just access it via the link
in the video description.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.520
The free version already gives you

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.080
basic understanding where you fall

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:53.970
into the adjusted grade distribution,

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:55.680
some basic statistics around that.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.540
And if you want even more insights,

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.060
there's the opportunity to
get a premium certificate

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.620
for a small additional sum.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.000
Next, let's talk about certificates

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.500
from online learning platforms,

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.600
like Udemy or Skillshare.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.240
I personally like these
platforms quite a lot.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:12.330
I also personally took many
courses on these platforms.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:13.620
And I'm actually also offering

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.770
some of my basic courses
on these platforms as well.

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:20.130
The reason why I put
them here, in the D tier,

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.300
is that actually I think,

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.040
while you might learn a lot of things,

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:26.430
it's not really respected
in the employer market.

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:27.690
And the reason is that often,

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.520
these certificates do not really have

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.500
proper examination structures.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:32.880
And this for me is the difference,

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.740
comparing these
certificates to certificates

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.470
from platforms like Udacity or Coursera,

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:39.420
where there are proper exams in the end.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:41.520
These types of examinations
just do not happen

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.050
for these types of online degrees.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:44.760
Which is why employers cannot really trust

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:45.660
that you have the skills.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.970
And of course, the
quality of these courses

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.440
can also differ quite a lot,

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:52.110
depending on the
instructor that you follow,

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.120
which is why I think
the D tier is justified.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:55.590
Next, let's talk about the CFI

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.230
and specifically the FMVA certification,

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:01.620
which is the Financial Modeling
and Valuation certification.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.990
And yes, this is a
quite industry specific,

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.910
function specific certificate.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.500
The reason why I'm mentioning it is,

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.660
because I think that many
people actually know it.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.700
Also just beyond the world of finance,

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.160
it just shows that you
have analytical skills.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:16.140
It shows that you are good in Excel,

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:18.093
good at modeling, good in data analysis,

00:09:18.093 --> 00:09:20.250
which is why I think that this is actually

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:21.450
something worth mentioning.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.070
And many people also from the community,

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:24.840
on Instagram told me that yes,

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:26.610
they know about the certification.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:28.680
And they felt that it really helped them

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.210
in their application process,

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.790
which is why I included
it here, in the B tier.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:36.420
Let's now talk about certifications
from business schools.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:38.160
These are certifications
that have recently,

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.280
in the last one or two years,
also seen lots of ads on.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.630
Business schools seem to promote

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.760
these certificates quite extensively.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:47.700
You can do certificates on
all types of different topics.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.580
General management, finance, blockchain,

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.310
crypto, sustainability, and so on.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.930
And often they're quite renowned

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:56.910
universities behind it, offering them.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.530
And then in a couple of weeks,

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.660
for a couple of thousand euros or dollars

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:01.710
that you need to pay,

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.330
you will get their certificate.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.010
And let's now start
talking about certificates

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:07.650
that are offered by Non-Target schools.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:11.490
So proper universities, but
not really Target schools.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:13.710
And frankly, here, I think
these types of certificates

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.660
are not that different from certificates

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:17.850
from platforms like Udacity, Coursera.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.800
The universities are not that renowned.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.720
Yes, it would likely be solid content

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.390
because it comes from an
established university.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.680
Often, there's also some type

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.720
of examination structure in the end.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.220
Which is why I decided to put them here

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:31.800
in the same tier, here in the C tier.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:34.080
And let's contrast that from
exactly these certificates

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.810
that are now offered from
Target business schools.

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:38.370
So certificates may be offered

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:41.940
by Harvard Business School,
by Stanford, by Wharton.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.690
Any of these other very
renowned business cools.

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.100
I think content wise,

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.390
maybe they're a little bit better,

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:49.440
maybe not, who knows.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:51.660
It probably depends on
the specific degree.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.580
Of course, now you have the advantage

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:57.690
of having this reputation, this
big bright name on your CV,

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:01.170
which maybe makes your CV
sparkle a little bit more.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.670
Frankly though, I think that there's

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:04.860
a very significant difference.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:08.310
Comparing such a certificate
that you maybe make at Harvard,

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.100
comparing it to a proper
bachelor degree at Harvard,

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.470
to a proper MBA at Harvard.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.770
How this will be perceived
is just very, very different.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:19.590
And the main reason is
that everyone will know

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:21.990
that actually, you just
paid yourself into it.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.520
Usually it's really not difficult

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:24.840
to get into these certificates.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.030
You just need to pay a
couple of thousand bucks

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:27.867
and then you can do it.

00:11:27.867 --> 00:11:30.090
You can write exams in the end.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:31.680
It's not really considered to be

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:34.470
a big achievement to have done that.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.330
You might learn some
good, interesting things.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:39.300
And yes, it might give a
little bit of a plus in the CV,

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.610
but don't expect that
only because you do that

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.620
this will really move your career forward

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:44.850
in a significant way.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.620
That's at least my humble opinion.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:48.150
Let me know in the
comments, if you have made

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:49.740
any other experiences on that.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.120
Next, let's talk about the GMAT,

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.580
the Graduate Management Ability Test.

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:56.430
And this might be a little
bit of a controversial choice

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:57.840
but I do think it's justified

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:00.090
to put the GMAT in the A tier.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.130
And maybe first, for the uninitiated,

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:05.340
the GMAT stands for General
Management Admission Test.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:07.410
It's an entry exam that is required

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.780
for many advanced business degrees,

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:12.780
including almost all renowned MBAs.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.550
And it consists of different sections.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:16.590
Integrated reasoning,
we need to make sense

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.510
of information that is presented to you.

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:21.960
Quantitative skills, we
need to do quant exercises.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:25.050
And also verbal logic
exercises that you need to do.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.930
So, first of all, I did the GMAT as well.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.930
When preparing for the GMAT for my MBAs,

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.700
actually I did learn a couple of things.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:35.280
I would argue that my
quant scales did improve

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:37.710
quite a bit just by preparing for the GMAT

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:38.970
in a structured way.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.700
Actually I made a video in the
past about my GMAT journey.

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.080
I will link it somewhere above here.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:44.850
Check it out if you're interested on that.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:47.220
But I do think that a strong GMAT score

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:49.020
and of course, the value
of the GMAT will be

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:51.090
very much determined by this score,

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:55.290
is a very strong indicator
towards employers.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.690
And I do think it can
help you to get the job,

00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:59.070
get that interview invitation.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:01.080
And it's not secret that
many consulting firms

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:05.100
actually ask in the application
forms for your GMAT score.

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:08.760
If you took one, they will want
to know what your score was.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:11.160
But of course don't make
yourself illusions here.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:14.940
If you have a score that
is below 650, for instance,

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.760
as an image just to provide
a couple of ballpark numbers,

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.610
this will likely more
hurt you, than help you.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:24.930
And then probably from
650 to 700, that's like,

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:28.140
you know it's like not really
good, not really that strong.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:29.550
Nothing that will really help you

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:31.110
to necessarily get invited.

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.780
If you score 700 or higher, this,

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:36.240
I'd say usually will be
considered a good score,

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.820
a solid score, where it will
definitely not hurt you.

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:40.500
Potentially then will also really show

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:43.530
your analytical ability,
your intellectual aptitude.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:46.290
But I'd say to really impress someone,

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:48.750
to really impress someone
with your GMAT score,

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:53.750
you need a score of 740,
750 ideally, or even higher.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.340
And then this will put you in the top 1%,

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:59.790
top 2%, top 3% of the test takers.

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.530
This is where you can
really impress people with.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:04.050
And if you do score above the 700s,

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:06.360
then I would argue for
many, many positions

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.190
this will help you quite a lot.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:10.350
Now let's talk about the one certification

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:12.630
that I would put into the S tier.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:16.980
And this is the CFA, the
Chartered Financial Analyst.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:19.650
And yes, this is a
certification that is of course,

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:22.220
based on one industry, on one function

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:23.910
in the finance function.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:25.440
And it is also true that actually

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.680
you can only hold this
certification in the end

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.800
if we work for, I believe
in four years or so,

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.210
in this area of business,

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:35.160
before that you will not even get it.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.170
But I would argue you don't even need

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:40.350
to have the full final CFA in the end.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:41.760
Just the fact that you completed

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.710
a CFA level one for instance,

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.450
or level two or level three.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.940
So three levels of exams,
you need to take level one

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.170
level two and level three.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.030
And then this is, I believe, how it works.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:52.110
If you have level three

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:53.820
and also meet these other requirements

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:55.620
like having a certain
amount of work experience

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.030
you will get the title.

00:14:57.030 --> 00:15:00.540
If you just have the first
levels, this already shows

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.790
that you have very good finance skills,

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:05.790
very good analytical, quantitative skills.

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:08.160
And the truth is, almost everyone

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:10.320
in the business community knows the CFA.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.470
Just a very well respected certification.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.690
Frankly, I look also
at my former colleagues

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:18.210
at McKinsey, what certifications they did.

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:20.832
Frankly, none of them had a PMP,

00:15:20.832 --> 00:15:22.290
at least as far as I'm aware.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:23.940
Almost none of them work maybe

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.220
with a SCRUM master or 6 Sigma belt.

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:28.170
Besides maybe the people really working

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:30.480
in the specialized practice in this area.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.700
But if you would look at
the CVs of these people,

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:35.880
quite a few of them had
actually CFAs completed

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.440
or at least the first levels.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:38.850
This is very common.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:40.920
The truth is also that the passing rates,

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:42.330
actually the failure rates,

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.280
of these CFA levels are quite high.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:47.310
For these certifications
about 50%, five zero

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:49.920
I believe, for the first
level even up to 60%,

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.650
six zero, of the people fail.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:55.440
Just showing that there is
a certain rigor behind it.

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:56.397
That not everyone gets it.

00:15:56.397 --> 00:15:58.110
You really need to prove your worth.

00:15:58.110 --> 00:15:59.670
Show what you are able to do.

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:01.290
But now all that being said,

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:02.910
do I think that you really need

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:05.700
these certifications
to succeed in business,

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:07.320
to advance your career?

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.220
And of course it's difficult

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:10.320
to give black and white answers on that.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.910
It might also depend on the environment,

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:13.530
the company that you apply for.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:16.980
But I'd argue, especially if
you apply for consulting roles,

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.660
also for investment banking.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:21.600
So these, let's say,
traditional high paced careers.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:25.110
Actually these certifications
are not really needed.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.960
I can promise you, you will not get hired

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:31.710
because you have these fancy
certifications on your resume.

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.810
If at all, if you have a very high GMAT

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.540
or maybe a strong CFA,
of course, this can help.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:39.120
This can underline your
analytical aptitude,

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:41.400
but I've never in my whole life

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:44.370
overheard any people say, oh this person,

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:47.370
this guy, this lady, such a strong person,

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:51.000
just to look at his or her
impressive certifications.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.160
This is just not how it works.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:55.080
So take all of this with a grain of salt.

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:57.750
Of course also this
ranking it's not a science,

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.460
just my personal judgment.

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:00.570
Let me know in the comments,

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.340
what your perspective on that is.

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:04.830
Very open to engage in
a conversation with you.

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:06.600
What I think is a nice little offering

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:09.480
is the CASE core certificate
that I talked about.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.940
The firm is actually also
sponsoring this video.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:15.300
Once again, you can download
your personal CASE certificate

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.670
in the most basic version for free.

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:19.110
Check out the link in
the video description

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:20.130
to get access to that.

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:22.110
It is quite respected by several employers

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:23.700
and available in many countries.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.170
So as always, if you took any value

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.430
out of this video at all,

